---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"A Planet You Can Take Apart: A Whole World as a Function and an Edit Log"}
  description={"About: A Planet You Can Take Apart. A planet whose every place and material can be explored cannot be stored; it can be computed on demand from a seed and an edit log, with only the ground near players simulated."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      A Planet You Can Take Apart: A Whole World as a Function and an Edit Log
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study asks what it takes to build a game in which every place on and inside a planet can be visited, dug into and examined down to the chemical elements in its rock. The arithmetic answers first: such a planet is far too large to store, so it has to be computed one position at a time from a seed, with a log of what players change, and only the ground near players can be simulated.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">In plain words</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>An Earth-sized planet at one byte per cubic metre would need about a zettabyte. No game can store that, so the planet must be a formula that answers "what is here?" for any position.</li>
        <li>Everything players change is kept as a list of edits on top of the formula. That list grows with play, not with the size of the planet.</li>
        <li>The formula and the edit list must give the same answer on every computer, or a tunnel dug on one machine opens into solid rock on another. Pictures of the planet only need to look right.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/planet/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/planet/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/planet.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
